    "markdown": "# Thematic evolution\n\n::: {.learning-objectives}\n**Learning objectives**\n\n- Select defensible time periods.\n- Examine theme continuity, emergence, splitting, and merging.\n- Distinguish genuinely emerging themes from sparse or declining themes.\n:::\n\n## Why one map is insufficient\n\nA cross-sectional thematic map combines the entire publication period. A topic that was central in 2010 and disappeared later may still appear prominent. Thematic evolution reconstructs the conceptual field within successive periods and links related themes across time [@cobo2011evolution; @aria2026evolution].\n\n## Choosing periods\n\nPeriods should satisfy three conditions:\n\n1. Each period contains enough publications and repeated terms.\n2. Cut-points are specified before viewing preferred results.\n3. The periods have a substantive or distributional rationale.\n\nPossible approaches include equal calendar periods, approximately equal document counts, or clinically meaningful milestones. Do not use annual slices when the network is sparse.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nsource(here::here(\"R\", \"00_setup.R\"))\nM <- load_demo_data()\n\nM <- M |>\n  dplyr::mutate(\n    DE = stringr::str_to_upper(stringr::str_squish(DE)),\n    ID = stringr::str_to_upper(stringr::str_squish(ID))\n  )\n\nM <- bibliometrix::mergeKeywords(M, force = TRUE)\n\nM |>\n  count(PY) |>\n  arrange(PY)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n     PY  n\n1  2008  2\n2  2009  2\n3  2010  7\n4  2011 10\n5  2012  6\n6  2013  6\n7  2014  6\n8  2015 12\n9  2016 12\n10 2017 13\n11 2018 15\n12 2019 14\n13 2020 22\n14 2021 32\n15 2022 26\n16 2023 25\n17 2024 24\n18 2025 26\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe teaching example uses cut-points at 2013, 2018, and 2022. These are provisional analytical choices for the synthetic corpus, not universal standards.\n\n## Run thematic evolution\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nM_complete <- M |>\n  filter(PY <= 2025)\n\nte <- bibliometrix::thematicEvolution(\n  M = M_complete,\n  field = \"KW_Merged\",\n  years = c(2013, 2018, 2022),\n  n = 100,\n  minFreq = 3,\n  size = 0.5,\n  ngrams = 1,\n  stemming = FALSE,\n  n.labels = 2,\n  repel = TRUE,\n  remove.terms = fcm_remove_terms,\n  synonyms = fcm_synonyms,\n  cluster = \"louvain\",\n  seed = 20261126\n)\n\nbibliometrix::plotThematicEvolution(\n  te$Nodes,\n  te$Edges,\n  min.flow = 0.10\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"plotly html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-b3468e86776fe6fdf601\" style=\"width:100%;height:464px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-b3468e86776fe6fdf601\">{\"x\":{\"visdat\":{\"31e84bf3bc6\":[\"function () \",\"plotlyVisDat\"]},\"cur_data\":\"31e84bf3bc6\",\"attrs\":{\"31e84bf3bc6\":{\"arrangement\":\"snap\",\"node\":{\"label\":[\"efficacy\",\"intravenous iron\",\"iron deficiency\",\"efficacy\",\"haemoglobin\",\"implementation\",\"iron deficiency\",\"iron-deficiency anaemia\",\"osteomalacia\",\"comparative effectiveness\",\"haemoglobin\",\"implementation\",\"parenteral therapy\",\"safety\",\"surgery\",\"treatment\",\"implementation\",\"iron-deficiency anaemia\",\"treatment\",\"iron deficiency\",\"safety\",\"length of stay\"],\"x\":[0,0,0,0.33333333333333331,0.33333333333333331,0.33333333333333331,0.33333333333333331,0.33333333333333331,0.33333333333333331,0.66666666666666663,0.66666666666666663,0.66666666666666663,0.66666666666666663,0.66666666666666663,0.66666666666666663,0.66666666666666663,1,1,1,1,1,1],\"y\":[0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001],\"color\":[