.48635335506229,61.09362005654819,67.687732080676881,41.539222717989212],\"color\":[\"#E41A1C80\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"rgba(0,0,0,0)\",\"#377EB880\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#4DAF4A80\",\"#984EA380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#984EA380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#D3D3D380\",\"#A6562880\",\"#F781BF80\",\"#66C2A580\"],\"customdata\":[[\"efficacy → efficacy\",0.3266866053072775],[\"efficacy → iron-deficiency anaemia\",0.45336580765944262],[\"intravenous iron → efficacy\",0.31873922867795701],[\"intravenous iron → haemoglobin\",0.16619707373626391],[\"intravenous iron → iron deficiency\",0.26290824082740161],[\"iron deficiency → implementation\",0.098632592025324373],[\"iron deficiency → iron deficiency\",0.62093143578175847],[\"iron deficiency → iron-deficiency anaemia\",0.16299903496267676],[\"efficacy → parenteral therapy\",0.36311008070040063],[\"efficacy → treatment\",0.27805890491106888],[\"haemoglobin → haemoglobin\",0.68019135821013177],[\"implementation → implementation\",0.68663989865242092],[\"iron deficiency → parenteral therapy\",0.56917243101875992],[\"iron deficiency → safety\",0.20990731535492818],[\"iron deficiency → treatment\",0.2080145784980319],[\"iron-deficiency anaemia → comparative effectiveness\",0.50888424986076886],[\"iron-deficiency anaemia → parenteral therapy\",0.23156666210090837],[\"osteomalacia → safety\",0.64571852605882851],[\"comparative effectiveness → implementation\",0.16388142314860263],[\"comparative effectiveness → iron-deficiency anaemia\",0.39649889289003909],[\"haemoglobin → treatment\",0.47902566749174524],[\"implementation → implementation\",0.62895182253369031],[\"parenteral therapy → iron deficiency\",0.65520660007399045],[\"parenteral therapy → iron-deficiency anaemia\",0.3244118612460124],[\"parenteral therapy → safety\",0.12486353355062291],[\"safety → safety\",0.61093620056548192],[\"surgery → length of stay\",0.67687732080676877],[\"treatment → treatment\",0.4153922271798921]],\"hovertemplate\":\"<b>%{customdata[0]}<\\/b><br>Lineage Strength: %{customdata[1]:.4f}<br><extra><\\/extra>\"},\"type\":\"sankey\",\"frame\":null}],\"highlight\":{\"on\":\"plotly_click\",\"persistent\":false,\"dynamic\":false,\"selectize\":false,\"opacityDim\":0.20000000000000001,\"selected\":{\"opacity\":1},\"debounce\":0},\"shinyEvents\":[\"plotly_hover\",\"plotly_click\",\"plotly_selected\",\"plotly_relayout\",\"plotly_brushed\",\"plotly_brushing\",\"plotly_clickannotation\",\"plotly_doubleclick\",\"plotly_deselect\",\"plotly_afterplot\",\"plotly_sunburstclick\"],\"base_url\":\"https://plot.ly\"},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n`minFreq` in `thematicEvolution()` is a minimum term frequency and is not the same argument definition as the lower-case `minfreq` used by `thematicMap()`.\n\n## Interpretation vocabulary\n\n| Pattern | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Continuation | A theme remains structurally related across periods |\n| Split | One earlier theme contributes to multiple later themes |\n| Merge | Multiple earlier themes contribute to one later theme |\n| Appearance | A theme has no meaningful predecessor under the chosen threshold |\n| Disappearance | A theme has no meaningful successor |\n\nA split or merge is a network result. It does not establish a clinical mechanism or causal change.\n\n## Emerging versus declining\n\nFor a lower-left theme, inspect:\n\n- first and last appearance;\n- annual term frequency;\n- publication count in the most recent complete period;\n- average publication year of representative documents;\n- continuation into the next period;\n- whether missing keywords or terminology changes explain the result.\n\nA new theme should show recent appearance or growth. A declining theme should show earlier prominence followed by reduced activity. A theme with two documents may simply be unstable.\n\n## Complement with term growth\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nselected_terms <- c(\n  \"heart failure\", \"pregnancy\", \"hypophosphataemia\",\n  \"cost effectiveness\", \"patient blood management\"\n)\n\nterm_growth <- M |>\n  select(PY, DE) |>\n  separate_rows(DE, sep = \";\") |>\n  mutate(DE = str_to_lower(str_squish(DE))) |>\n  filter(DE %in% selected_terms) |>\n  count(PY, DE)\n\nggplot(term_growth, aes(PY, n, colour = DE)) +\n  geom_line(linewidth = 0.9) +\n  geom_point() +\n  labs(x = \"Year\", y = \"Keyword occurrences\", colour = \"Term\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](06-thematic-evolution_files/figure-html/evolution-term-growth-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Exercise\n\nRepeat the evolution analysis using one alternative set of cut-points. Record which lineages are preserved and which are sensitive to period construction.\n\n",
